   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "Relay Four is an unmanned microwave hut on a forested ridge: a concrete equipment shelter, a 20 m guyed tower with its dishes, a fenced compound round the propane tank and a helipad the phone company used twice a year. When the Cordon closed the roads off the mountain it took the hut over to pass its orders from checkpoint to checkpoint, and posted a two-man signals team on it: Sergeant Reyes and Specialist Hale. Their relief never came. Hale let three hikers in off the trail against orders, and the coughing one brought the Bloom with him; Reyes shut the other two in the generator room with the heat. A dispatch rider who carried the last sheet of orders up the track stayed the night and never left. The last order was to burn the code books and hold the post. Reyes burned them, locked the ammunition and the spare codes in the battery room, carried the key up the tower where the Hollowed can't climb, and went down to sit with the batteries because it was warm in there. The tank reads empty now and the dishes are dark.",
